ription: Starting from April 1st 2024 third-party cookies will be restricted on Google Chrome and Microsoft Edge. This restriction can block the access to content that runs in the site iframe and doesn’t use SAP-managed domains such as ondemand.com or cloud.sap. Namely, it will affect non-SAP content, sites that are using a full custom domain, and sites that are using a standalone appRouter such as in the case of a launchpad module.  To avoid this situation, customers can apply to participate in the first-party deprecation trial, and request Google to issue them a token that will temporarily re-enable third-party cookies until December 27th, 2024”. For more information, see Request more time to prepare with the third-party cookie deprecation trial for top-level sites.  Action:  If affected, customers should get familiar with the deprecation trial program and request a token from Google. Once the token is issued, they should open a support ticket on component EP-WZ-DMN and provide SAP the token details.  Official SAP Note: 3409306 . \nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-26\nValid as Of: 2024-04-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3202 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Third Party Cookies Deprecation\nDescription: Starting from April 1st 2024 third-party cookies will be restricted on Google Chrome and Microsoft Edge. This restriction can block the access to content that runs in the site iframe and doesn’t use SAP-managed domains such as ondemand.com or cloud.sap. Namely, it will affect non-SAP content, sites that are using a full custom domain, and sites that are using a standalone appRouter such as in the case of a launchpad module.  To avoid this situation, customers can apply to participate in the first-party deprecation trial, and request Google to issue them a token that will temporarily re-enable third-party cookies until December 27th, 2024. For more information, see Request more time to prepare with the third-party cookie deprecation trial for top-level sites.  Action:  If affected, customers should get familiar with the deprecation trial program and request a token from Google. Once the token is issued, they should open a support ticket on component EP-WZ-DMN and provide SAP the token details.  Official SAP Note: 3409306 . \nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3203 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Third Party Cookies Deprecation\nDescription: Starting from April 1st 2024 third-party cookies will be restricted on Google Chrome and Microsoft Edge. This restriction can block the access to content that runs in the site iframe and doesn’t use SAP-managed domains such as ondemand.com or cloud.sap. Namely, it will affect non-SAP content, sites that are using a full custom domain, and sites that are using a standalone appRouter such as in the case of a launchpad module.  To avoid this situation, customers can apply to participate in the first-party deprecation trial, and request Google to issue them a token that will temporarily re-enable third-party cookies until December 27th, 2024. For more information, see Request more time to prepare with the third-party cookie deprecation trial for top-level sites.  Action:  If affected, customers should get familiar with the deprecation trial program and request a token from Google. Once the token is issued, they should open a support ticket on component EP-WZ-DMN and provide SAP the token details.  Official SAP Note: 3409306 . \nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3204 ---\nComponent: Business Data Orchestration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create a Destination with Client Certificate Authentication\nDescription: You can use client certificate authentication to establish an HTTP connection between your Business Data Orchestration application running on an SAP BTP, ABAP environmentt and an SAP Destination service configured for \"ClientCertificateAuthentication\". See Create a Destination with Client Certificate Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3205 ---\nComponent: Business Data Orchestration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Display Clients\nDescription: You can now display read-only information of all clients connected to an SAP Master Data Integration tenant. For more information, see Display Clients.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3206 ---\nComponent: Business Data Orchestration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Rebranding Changes\nDescription: We have renamed the SAP Master Data Orchestration. The service will now be referred to as Business Data Orchestration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed", "Line of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3206 ---\nComponent: Business Data Orchestration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Rebranding Changes\nDescription: We have renamed the SAP Master Data Orchestration. The service will now be referred to as Business Data Orchestration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3207 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Avai